WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.021 --> 00:00:01.909
(bouncy chiming music)

00:00:01.909 --> 00:00:06.197
- [Narrator] This is Koda, a
three-year-old African cheetah.

00:00:06.197 --> 00:00:10.364
Critically endangered, less
than 8,000 remain in the wild.

00:00:12.759 --> 00:00:15.063
The African cheetah is built for speed.

00:00:15.063 --> 00:00:17.158
It's the world's fastest land animal,

00:00:17.158 --> 00:00:21.824
clocking zero to 60 miles per
hour in a mere 3.4 seconds.

00:00:21.824 --> 00:00:23.955
Long and lean with a flexible spine,

00:00:23.955 --> 00:00:25.856
they use their tail as a rudder,

00:00:25.856 --> 00:00:28.346
steering when running after prey.

00:00:28.346 --> 00:00:30.344
They stalk their prey under the bright sun

00:00:30.344 --> 00:00:32.253
of the African Savanna.

00:00:32.253 --> 00:00:34.200
The tear marks that run across their face

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.302
help reflect the glare of the
sun much like football players

00:00:37.302 --> 00:00:40.571
apply paint beneath
their eyes before a game.

00:00:40.571 --> 00:00:42.971
They once roamed across all of Africa,

00:00:42.971 --> 00:00:44.973
but today are found in less than a quarter

00:00:44.973 --> 00:00:47.332
of their historic range.

00:00:47.332 --> 00:00:49.837
Habitat loss, poaching, and loss of prey

00:00:49.837 --> 00:00:53.004
are all threats to this beautiful cat.

00:00:55.162 --> 00:00:57.579
This is the African cheetah.

